                Chancellor’s gold medals were awarded to Deep Deka, MCA and Tanmayee Devchoudhury, BA English. Five Salvers: Prof Mihir Kanti Chaudhuri Best Science Graduate Award went to Bhaswati Goswami, MSc Botany; Sanwarmal Modi Award for Excellence in Cultural Activities went to Akhit Nayan Gogoi, B Pharma; Gini Devi Pansari Award for excellence in Literary Activities went to Dhiman Chakraborty, B.Sc. Geology; Basudeo Pansari Award for Excellence in Community Service went to Sagar Kumar Nag, BA Administrative Service; and Suresh Kumar Prithani Award for Excellence in Mentoring went to Bidisha Kashyap, BA Political science. Apart from this, 56 gold medals and 58 silver medals were presented to successful students from various departments of the university.
                <br><br>
                The Honorary Doctor of Science Degree was conferred upon Dr Naresh Trehan for his pioneering contributions to cardiac science and service to healthcare. Sri Sanjiv Goenka received Honorary Doctor of Letters for his contribution to education, nation-building and public welfare. Sri Yeshe Dorjee Thongchi was conferred with Honorary Doctor of Literature in recognition of his lifetime devotion to literature enriching the region’s literary heritage while Honorary Doctor of Law was awarded to Sri Mahesh Agarwal for his dedication to advancement of justice and the public good.
                <br><br>
                The Convocation began with the grand and elegant Academic Procession, which was participated by the Registrar of the University, Academic Council members, members of Board of Governors, Deans of different schools, Heads of different Departments, and the Award recipients. The Convocation ended with the signing of the National Anthem.
